    {
      "id": "ptmgw0o",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.2 Agriculture :The Backbone"
    },
    {
      "id": "ko9ahtt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4.2.1 The Green Revolution"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vzj0s03",
      "content": "Punjab became the 'Granary of India' or 'Breadbasket of India' through the Green Revolution of the 1960s–70s. Key facts:"
    },
    {
      "id": "i2zaqtd",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Aspect</p>",
            "<p>Details</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Period</p>",
            "<p>Mid-1960s to 1970s</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Key Architect</p>",
            "<p>Dr. M.S. Swaminathan (Norman Borlaug for wheat varieties globally)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>New Varieties</p>",
            "<p>HYV (High-Yielding Varieties) :Kalyan Sona and Sonalika for wheat; IR-8 for rice</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Institutional Support</p>",
            "<p>Bhakra-Nangal Dam for irrigation; IARI (Indian Agricultural Research Institute) for research</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Results</p>",
            "<p>Punjab's wheat production rose from ~2 MT (1960s) to 17+ MT; rice production expanded massively</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Punjab's contribution</p>",
            "<p>Punjab produces ~17–19% of India's wheat and ~11% of India's rice on just 1.6% of land</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Negative Effects</p>",
            "<p>Waterlogging, soil degradation, pesticide overuse, groundwater depletion, burning of stubble (parali), monoculture dependence</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Agriculture is the backbone of Punjab's economy, driving growth and ensuring national food security.",
      "id": "8kxenm3"
    },
